# Code owners — who is asked to review a change, by folder.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the matching owner on every pull request that
# touches a path. The ruleset on `main` turns that request into a requirement
# once a second maintainer has accepted the organization invitation (a sole
# owner cannot approve their own change).
#
# Two roles, mirroring the pattern in docs/ENTERPRISE.md:
#   registry-maintainers — the record and everything built from it
#   the architecture owner — the rules, the checks, and the publishing job
#
# Order matters: the last matching line wins.

# Default: every change is seen by the maintainers.
*                       @Aina-Design-Corp/registry-maintainers

# The record and what is built from it
/registry/              @Aina-Design-Corp/registry-maintainers
/intake/                @Aina-Design-Corp/registry-maintainers
/site/                  @Aina-Design-Corp/registry-maintainers
/docs/                  @Aina-Design-Corp/registry-maintainers

# The rules, the checks, and the publishing job
/schemas/               @joehagedorn
/scripts/               @joehagedorn
/.github/               @joehagedorn
/package.json           @joehagedorn

# This file itself
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @joehagedorn
